  "presentation_summary": [
    "69-year-old man with type 2 diabetes and hypertension presented in August with headache followed by diplopia.",
    "Headache began about 1 week earlier in the right occiput and moved toward the right orbit; diplopia began 5 days later.",
    "He had hiked in rural New York State 1 month before presentation but denied tick bite, rash, fever, or chills.",
    "Exam showed left cranial nerve III palsy with otherwise normal neurologic and physical examination. Brain MRI/MRA were negative.",
    "CSF showed WBC 74/uL with 84% lymphocytes/atypical lymphocytes, protein 77 mg/dL, and glucose 101 mg/dL. Serum and CSF Lyme testing supported neuroborreliosis. Headache resolved with ceftriaxone and diplopia resolved by 2 months."
